=== information bars toy (AFML ch.2; teaching only, NO HFT recipe) ===
cite: López de Prado AFML ch.2 — tick/volume/dollar bars vs time bars
params: synthetic tick stream seed=0; n_ticks=5000; time_bar=50 ticks wall; tick_bar=50 trades; vol_bar=200 shares; dollar_bar≈200*mid
clock comparison on SAME synthetic tick tape:
time/tick50  n_bars= 100 mean_|ret|=0.004509 std_ret=0.005825 max_gap_s=50
volume200    n_bars= 241 mean_|ret|=0.002966 std_ret=0.003627 max_gap_s=28
dollar~200p  n_bars= 231 mean_|ret|=0.003033 std_ret=0.003760 max_gap_s=28
teach: time bars sample the clock; tick/volume/dollar bars sample activity — busy periods mint more bars, quiet periods fewer. This is a sampling choice for research bars, NOT a latency or HFT execution recipe.
intuition: if news hits and 1000 trades arrive in one minute, time bars still emit one 1-min bar, while tick/volume/dollar bars emit many — returning the series closer to an 'information clock'.
toy_counts {'time50': 100, 'vol200': 241, 'dollar': 231}

=== mask-first / upstream contamination (arXiv:2507.07107; optional conservative protocol (toy)) ===
protocol_label: this toy DELIBERATELY sets limit rows as non-executable and combines obs/quality/trade into one conservative M; not a market law (see three-mask section below)
cite: https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.07107 — upstream contamination: limit closes enter rolling ops BEFORE row filter
paper_ablation_cite: no-mask apparent IC +18% while realised Sharpe −0.44 vs full mask (author ablation)
REJECT_as_course_alpha: Sharpe 2.05 synthetic / 1.63 real; 213-factor GPU engine; AdjMSE γ system
params: toy seed=11; T=750; N=120; limit_up_p≈0.04; mom_window=10; fantasy vs realisable fill
toy_IC_apparent_contam 0.0264
toy_IC_realisable_contam 0.0053
toy_IC_mask_first 0.0017
toy_IC_inflate_apparent_vs_realisable_pct 394.0
toy_SR_fantasy_contam 3.007
toy_SR_realisable_contam 0.914
toy_SR_mask_first 0.814
toy_SR_gap_fantasy_minus_realisable 2.093
teach: contaminated rolling features make limit-chasing look predictive (high apparent IC / fantasy SR); realisable fill on the same features collapses — under this toy protocol the combined M refuses closes the toy marks non-executable.
toy_protocol_M: M[t,i] = obs AND quality AND trade (toy-set; conservative research choice, not a general rule); rolling ops here ignore M=0; post-hoc row drop CANNOT un-poison aggregates already computed.

